item.text:
**Reused evidence**
REUSE_JSON: {"evidence_ids":["E0001"],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.6","7B.7"]}
Khamenei’s constitutional command-and-appointment authority is the main baseline for ruler attribution in this chapter, especially for scrutiny, censorship, and protection from accountability.

**New evidence**
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iran's Khamenei says economy should not be tied to U.S. sanctions","publisher":"Reuters via Yahoo News","publication_date":"2022-03-21","url":"https://www.yahoo.com/news/irans-khamenei-says-economy-not-135316587.html","claim":"Khamenei said Iran should not tie its economy to lifting U.S. sanctions and urged officials to govern so sanctions would not hurt the country, while promoting a knowledge-based economy.","locator":"opening paragraphs and quoted remarks","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire with direct quotations from Khamenei and clear date/setting.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Khamenei public statement.","contrary_evidence":["This is policy rhetoric, not proof of truthfulness or delivery.","It can be read as strategic framing rather than a factual claim about economic conditions."],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2","7B.8","7B.10"]}
- Khamenei’s own public line here is more about framing and blame-shifting than measurable candor, but it is still relevant because he explicitly told the public to decouple the economy from sanctions relief.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Khamenei Says Iran's Future Should Not Be Tied to Nuclear Talks","publisher":"Voice of America / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-04-13","url":"https://www.voanews.com/a/khamenei-says-iran-s-future-should-not-be-tied-to-nuclear-talks-/6528929.html","claim":"Khamenei said Iran’s future should not depend on the success or collapse of nuclear talks and told officials not to wait for negotiations when planning the country.","locator":"reported remarks from senior officials gathering","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting with a specific attributable statement and date.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Khamenei public statement.","contrary_evidence":["This does not by itself show deception; it may simply be a negotiating posture.","It does not establish whether his public framing matched internal policy constraints."],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2","7B.8","7B.10"]}
- This is useful mainly as a truthfulness/commitment indicator: he publicly downplayed the centrality of nuclear talks while maintaining a hard line.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iran's Khamenei says Western enemies stoking anti-hijab protests","publisher":"Reuters via Yahoo News","publication_date":"2022-07-27","url":"https://www.yahoo.com/news/irans-khamenei-says-western-enemies-142859415.html","claim":"Khamenei accused Western adversaries of being behind women activists challenging Iran’s dress code and said enemy media were attacking Iran to spread doubt.","locator":"opening paragraphs and quoted remarks","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire with direct quotations and clear identification of the speech context.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Khamenei public statement.","contrary_evidence":["The statement is political blame-shifting, not a verified factual account.","It is not proof of personal gain or hidden corruption."],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2","7B.8","7B.10"]}
- This supports a recurring pattern of externalizing blame and presenting internal dissent as foreign manipulation.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iran's Khamenei blames Israel, US in first comments on protests","publisher":"Al Jazeera / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-10-03","url":"https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2022/10/3/irans-khamenei-blames-israel-us-in-first-comments-on-protests","claim":"In his first public comments on the protests, Khamenei called them riots, blamed the United States and Israel, and said the death of Mahsa Amini had broken his heart while still denying that the unrest reflected normal public reaction.","locator":"middle paragraphs containing the quoted speech","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters-reported speech with direct quotation and strong contemporaneous corroboration.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Khamenei public statement.","contrary_evidence":["He did acknowledge Amini’s death as painful, which is a limited sign of acknowledgment.","The speech still sharply shifted responsibility away from the state and toward foreign enemies."],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2","7B.8","7B.10"]}
- The one partial positive here is acknowledgment of pain over Amini’s death; the dominant feature is the move to deny domestic responsibility and recast unrest as foreign-instigated.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iran's Khamenei calls anti-government protests 'scattered riots' designed by the enemy","publisher":"Euronews / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-10-13","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/10/13/iran-women-khamenei","claim":"Khamenei described the protests as scattered riots designed by the enemy and said the unrest was a clumsy foreign plot against the Iranian nation.","locator":"first paragraphs of the Reuters wire","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire reproduced by a major outlet, with direct attribution to Khamenei’s remarks.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Khamenei public statement.","contrary_evidence":["Still rhetorical rather than documentary proof of deliberate falsehood.","It reinforces the same blame-shifting pattern already seen in October."],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2","7B.8","7B.10"]}
- This is largely cumulative with the October 3 speech, but it helps show repetition rather than an isolated comment.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iran leader says 'enemies' may target workers as protests rage","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-11-19","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/world-news/iran-leader-says-enemies-may-target-workers-as-protests-rage-2948267","claim":"Khamenei warned that Iran’s enemies may try to mobilize workers after failing to topple the Islamic government, framing the protest movement as a hostile external campaign.","locator":"opening paragraph and speech summary","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire summary, though the mirror is less direct than Reuters itself.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Khamenei public statement.","contrary_evidence":["The claim remains political framing, not a tested factual report.","It does not by itself show concealment or self-enrichment."],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2","7B.8","7B.10"]}
- The repeated “enemy” framing matters here because it is a public effort to delegitimize domestic dissent rather than answer it.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iran's Khamenei praises Basij forces for confronting 'riots'","publisher":"Reuters via VOA","publication_date":"2022-11-27","url":"https://www.voanews.com/amp/iran-s-khamenei-praises-basij-forces-for-confronting-riots-/6851488.html","claim":"Khamenei praised Basij forces for sacrificing themselves to save people from rioters, explicitly endorsing the militia wing that was central to protest suppression.","locator":"first paragraphs of the Reuters wire","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire with direct quotation and clear context.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Khamenei public statement.","contrary_evidence":["This is supportive of repression, not evidence of personal honesty.","It helps mainly as evidence of tolerance and endorsement of the crackdown narrative."],"lenses":["7B.2","7B.7","7B.10"]}
- This is the clearest target-year item for 7B.7: he publicly legitimized the coercive network rather than distancing himself from it.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Treasury Sanctions Iranian Leaders Responsible for Internet Shutdown and Violent Crackdown on Peaceful Protests","publisher":"U.S. Department of the Treasury","publication_date":"2022-10-06","url":"https://home.treasury.gov/news/press-releases/jy0994","claim":"OFAC said seven senior leaders in Iran’s government and security apparatus were responsible for shutting down Iran’s internet access and continuing violence against peaceful protesters; the release specifically named the interior minister, communications minister, and an IRGC-linked close associate of the Supreme Leader’s orbit.","locator":"main release text and sanctions rationale sections","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary U.S. government sanctions notice with specific named roles and rationale.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but material: the named officials acted inside the Khamenei-led system; not a direct personal order from Khamenei in the document.","contrary_evidence":["The document does not name Khamenei himself as the actor.","It is a sanctions finding, so it is adversarial but still primary evidence."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7","7B.10"]}
- This is useful as evidence that the regime used state power to suppress scrutiny and access to information.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Treasury Sanctions Iranian Officials and Entities Responsible for Ongoing Crackdown on Protests and Internet Censorship","publisher":"U.S. Department of the Treasury","publication_date":"2022-10-26","url":"https://home.treasury.gov/news/press-releases/jy1048","claim":"OFAC said additional Iranian officials and entities were involved in the ongoing crackdown on protests and efforts to disrupt digital freedom, including internet throttling, surveillance, and arrests of dissidents.","locator":"opening release text and IRGC Intelligence Organization sections","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary government sanction notice with detailed attribution to specific bodies and conduct.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but material: the conduct is within the apparatus Khamenei oversees, though the document does not specify his direct personal order.","contrary_evidence":["This is still institutional attribution, not a personal confession or asset disclosure.","It proves repression and concealment more clearly than financial self-dealing."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7","7B.10"]}
- This reinforces that the state’s response to scrutiny was coercive rather than transparent.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"U.S. Treasury Issues Iran General License D-2 to Increase Support for Internet Freedom","publisher":"U.S. Department of the Treasury","publication_date":"2022-09-23","url":"https://home.treasury.gov/news/press-releases/jy0974","claim":"Treasury said the Iranian government cut off internet access for most citizens to prevent the world from watching its crackdown on peaceful protesters, and the license was issued to help Iranians access outside platforms and services.","locator":"opening paragraphs and Deputy Secretary quotation","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary U.S. government statement with explicit causal language about concealment.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but material: the action is attributed to the Iranian government under Khamenei’s system.","contrary_evidence":["The document is a U.S. policy statement, not an internal Iranian record.","It does not isolate Khamenei personally from the broader regime action."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7","7B.10"]}
- The “prevent the world from watching” language is especially relevant to 7B.7 because it links censorship to concealment of abuse.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"As unrest grows, Iran restricts access to Instagram, WhatsApp","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-09-21","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/world-news/as-unrest-grows-iran-restricts-access-to-instagram-whatsapp-2896618","claim":"Iran restricted access to Instagram and WhatsApp as protests grew after Mahsa Amini’s death, according to residents and NetBlocks, limiting key public communication channels.","locator":"opening paragraphs","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire with contemporaneous technical reporting and named platforms.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but material: the restriction was imposed by the Iranian state apparatus under Khamenei’s authority.","contrary_evidence":["This is an implementation fact, not a statement of intent from Khamenei.","It shows censorship rather than personal enrichment."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7","7B.10"]}
- This is the clearest operational censorship evidence in the target year.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Exclusive: Reuters investigates business empire of Iran's supreme leader","publisher":"Reuters via Yahoo News","publication_date":"2013-11-11","url":"https://www.yahoo.com/news/exclusive-reuters-investigates-business-empire-irans-supreme-leader-101119485.html","claim":"Reuters reported that Khamenei controlled Setad, a vast business empire worth about $95 billion, and that the organization expanded under him with final resources independent of parliament and the national budget.","locator":"middle and later paragraphs on Setad’s scope, control, and lack of supervision","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Major Reuters investigation with detailed documentary and interview basis, though not in the target year.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Pre-2022 structural background that still frames the 2022 period.","ruler_attribution":"Strong for long-running Khamenei control over the structure; not proof of personal cash enrichment.","contrary_evidence":["Reuters said there was no evidence Khamenei personally tapped Setad to enrich himself.","Because it predates 2022, it is background rather than target-period conduct."],"lenses":["7B.3","7B.4","7B.5","7B.7","7B.9","7B.10"]}
- This is important context for conflicts of interest and opaque power, even though it is not a target-year event.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Conglomerate controlled by Iran's supreme leader a winner from nuclear deal","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2015-07-14","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/world-news/conglomerate-controlled-by-iran%27s-supreme-leader-a-winner-from-nuclear-deal-361546","claim":"Reuters reported that Setad was close to Iran’s ruling elite, that Khamenei exerted exclusive control over its economic empire and chose its executives, and that the structure was used to fund hardline leverage and bypass normal government branches.","locator":"paragraphs describing Setad’s control and governance","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting with explicit attribution and structural detail.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Structural background relevant to 2022, though published earlier.","ruler_attribution":"Strong for Khamenei’s control over the Setad network; still not a personal asset disclosure.","contrary_evidence":["The article also says Reuters found no evidence of personal enrichment.","Its date means it should be used as inherited-structure context, not fresh 2022 conduct."],"lenses":["7B.3","7B.4","7B.5","7B.7","7B.9","7B.10"]}
- This is the best source for the appointment/control side of the integrity chapter, because it says he chose executives and kept exclusive control.

**Search and rejection summary**
I reviewed roughly 30 documents across Reuters wires and mirrors, Treasury sanctions notices, VOA, Al Jazeera, Euronews, and older Reuters investigations on Setad. I kept the highest-value non-duplicative items and rejected several groups:
- Duplicate protest articles that repeated the same Khamenei remarks without adding new claims.
- Purely 3B/4B items about repression, arrests, and internet shutdowns when they did not add a personal-integrity nexus.
- Later 2023 schoolgirl-poisoning stories, which were outside the 2022 target period.
- Generic country corruption indicators and inherited authoritarian context that do not by themselves prove Khamenei’s personal dishonesty.
- Repeated Reuters mirror copies of the same wire when the underlying claim was already captured once.
- Broad commentary on Iran’s elite politics that lacked a ruler-specific honesty, conflict-of-interest, or concealment claim.

**Remaining gaps**
- Direct 2022 evidence of Khamenei’s own assets, gifts, or personal financial benefit is still thin. The Setad material shows control and opaque power, but not personal enrichment.
- There is little direct evidence of him admitting error or correcting false claims in 2022.
- More target-year material on appointments, family access, and any documented intervention in procurement, licensing, or enforcement would help 7B.3 to 7B.6.
- A tighter 2022 trail from Khamenei’s office to specific censorship or investigative obstruction decisions would strengthen the 7B.7 attribution.
- If you want a stronger integrity dossier, the next useful search would be on official transcripts of Khamenei’s 2022 speeches, sanctions findings about his office-linked entities, and investigative reporting on Mojtaba Khamenei or other office-linked intermediaries in 2022.
